{title: 380 - Welcome, Day of Sweet Repose}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #380 • EVANS • 7.5.7.8}
{lyricist: LH. Evans}
{composer: L A. Steinel}
{key: Db}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 380}
{meta: tune EVANS}
{meta: meter 7.5.7.8}
{meta: category Doctrines - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Db]Welcome, day of [Gb]sweet [Bbm/F]repose!
[Db]Blessed be [Gb]thy [Db/Ab]sacred [Ab7]hours!
[Ab]We would [Bbm]trust [Eb7/Db]the [Ab/C]One who [Ab7/Gb]knows
[Fm]All our weak [Ab7/Gb]and [Gb]failing [Ab7]powers.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Db]Welcome, day in [Gb]Eden [Ebm]born!
[Db]Holy [Gb]rest for [Db/Ab]sinless man!
[Ab]Like the [Bbm]dawning [Ab/C]of fair [Ab7/Gb]morn
[Fm]Come thy [Ab7/Gb]hours [Gb]to [Db/Ab]us [Ab7]again.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Db]Welcome, day blessed [Gb]by [Bbm/F]our [Ebm]Lord!
[Db]Toil shall [Gb]cease and [Db/Ab]anxious care.
[Ab]Day commanded by His [Ab7/Gb]word,
[Fm]Day for [Ab7/Gb]song [Gb]and [Db/Ab]praise [Ab7]and [Db]prayer.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Db]Welcome, day our [Gb]Savior [Ebm]kept!
[Db]Keeping, [Gb]wrought our [Db/Ab]righteousness,
[Ab]Day God [Bbm]bids [Eb7/Db]us [Ab/C]ne'er forget,
[Fm]Day of [Ab7/Gb]days [Gb]His [Db/Ab]name [Ab7]to [Db]bless.
{end_of_verse}
